  "cards": [
    {
      "title": "Read from the centre",
      "items": [
        "The reference server is the system under test. Surrounding boxes identify who controls it, which actors exchange protocols with it, and where evidence goes.",
        "The bench harness groups the CLI, scenario runner and supervisor. The server groups the shared runtime and application; these are logical roles, not extra processes.",
        "Owned runtimes can run embedded or as a built process. The supervisor waits for readiness and stops the runtime before closing fixtures; attaching to an existing HTTPS server skips runtime ownership."
      ],
      "dot": "neutral"
    },
    {
      "title": "Two different environments",
      "items": [
        "Simulated runs combine a synthetic device with local Apple-service fixtures. Live runs use real credentials and the appropriate real services.",
        "Contract suites exercise interfaces directly and write their own Go test output. Their results do not flow into bench JSON/JUnit reports."
      ],
      "dot": "neutral"
    },
    {
      "title": "Reading and protocol references",
      "items": [
        "Lab scope and operation — https://github.com/deploymenttheory/go-apple-dm/blob/main/docs/testing/lab.md",
        "Go test behavior — https://pkg.go.dev/cmd/go#hdr-Test_packages",
        "Sending MDM commands — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/devicemanagement/sending-mdm-commands-to-a-device",
        "Sending APNs requests — https://developer.apple.com/documentation/usernotifications/sending-notification-requests-to-apns"
      ],
      "dot": "transport"
    }
